study_1/43856_2025_810_MOESM2_ESM.pdf.md:5:Figure  S1.  Flowchart  of  Cerebellar  Segmentation  Process  for  Patients. The preprocessing  of  patients'  MRI  3D  T1  images  was  conducted  to  remove  the brainstem  region  and  prevent  erroneous  segmentation  of  the  enlarged  brainstem. First, the brainstem was manually delineated using the "Draw" tool in MRIcron, and the marked region was saved as a VOI file. The "Draw/Advanced/Subtraction Plots" function  was  then  used  to  subtract  the  marked  brainstem  region  from  the  original image, resulting in brainstem-excluded images. Next, the preprocessed images were imported  into  the  ACAPULCO  software  package,  where  the  cerebellum  was automatically  segmented,  including  region  localization  and  lobular  segmentation. Two  neurosurgery  specialists  independently  reviewed  the  segmented  images  to ensure  accuracy.  Any  segmentation  inaccuracies  were  manually  corrected,  and  the final results were determined through consensus. Cases that could not be corrected manually or involved significant discrepancies were excluded. Due to the variability in the segmentation boundaries of lobules VIIIA and VIIIB across participants, these two lobules were merged into a single lobule (VIII). Finally, the volumes of the 26 cerebellar lobules were calculated based on the corrected segmentation maps.
